    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d823">

                <pb facs="0906" n="786" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg786"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Ambassador
                    McCormick.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-02-14"><hi rendition="#italic">February 14,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay advises Mr. McCormick that the three officers of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lena</hi>, Midshipman Peter Michailoff, Midshipman
                    Andrey Kyra Dinyan, and Engineer Sergey Kapazin, who broke their parole toward
                    the end of January, are reported to have arrived at St. Petersburg and to have
                    reported to the admiralty. Instructs him to inform the Russian Government and to
                    inquire what action it proposes to take.)</p>
            </div>
